# I. Executive verdict

**The central mathematics survives this audit. The current manuscript is not yet journal-submission ready. Its strongest defensible publication form is a focused synthesis or methodological article, not a paper whose case rests on a newly discovered Boolean algebra or a substantial new classification theorem.**

The manuscript contributes an organized symbolic/numeric calculus: a numeric truth matrix is transported into a formula-valued polarity matrix; logical pairing becomes evaluation on agreement bits; valuation, pointwise Boolean composition and input-frame changes fit together. The invertible frame normal form and partition-selector characterization are the most effective explanations of that organization. They remain valid when the reference formulas are dependent or contradictory. The arbitrary-arity results follow from general Boolean identities, rather than from a conjectural extrapolation of binary examples.

No central false theorem was found. The present source has repaired the earlier polarity-mask inconsistency, states the all-true valuation qualification, specifies ordered flattenings, separates output complement from unchanged-outer-operation frame transport, and correctly uses ordinary $\mathbb F_2$ rank. The remaining mathematical work is mainly precision: explicitly specify the combined symbolic signed-frame action, expand one compressed higher-arity proof step, and remove a local row/column inconsistency in the STP comparison.

The novelty case is narrower than the amount of notation might suggest. Cheng, Zhao and Xu directly state the numeric truth-vector composition law [S1]. Bricken gives earlier binary matrix and bra--matrix--ket logic [S2]. Boolean-algebra-valued matrix and orthogonal-frame constructions give a close antecedent for the formula frame itself [S3]. The general coherence package is explained by Boolean homomorphisms and pullbacks. This does not make the manuscript useless: a well-designed representation and teaching/specification architecture can be publishable. It does mean that its usefulness must be demonstrated, not inferred from the number of theorem environments.

**The 20,873-check assertion is not reproducible from the supplied package.** Its two-line output survives, but the associated generating program, count definition and execution recipe were not located after recursive archive inspection. A separate checker written for this audit passes **2,022,648 explicitly counted checks**. That new result independently supports the finite claims; it does not establish the provenance of the old run.

