# XVIII. Suggested contribution language

## Replacement contribution paragraph

We present a formula-valued representation calculus for Boolean functions with explicit reference frames. A logical matrix is the polarity orbit of a reference formula, and its frame normal form relates it to the corresponding numeric truth matrix by invertible Boolean matrices. Logical pairing evaluates the represented connective on agreement with the reference formulas. These constructions fit into a common system of compatibility laws: valuation, aligned pointwise Boolean composition, input-frame transport and pairing preserve the same Boolean operations. The calculus extends to arbitrary-arity truth tensors and ordered rectangular flattenings, where ordinary field rank measures XOR-conjunctive separability across a chosen variable partition. The aim is a precise and usable symbolic/numeric organization of classical Boolean mechanisms, rather than a new Boolean algebra, physical measurement theory or compression scheme.

## Replacement novelty/related-work paragraph

Truth-vector composition, logical matrix evaluation, Boolean orthogonal expansions, input-frame transformations and matrix rank factorization have substantial prior literature. In particular, aligned numeric pointwise composition is already explicit in Cheng, Zhao and Xu, while Boolean-algebra-valued frame constructions provide a close antecedent for the complementary frame matrices used here. The contribution pursued in this paper is the integrated reference-polarity presentation and its explicit agreement-pairing and transport contracts. We therefore distinguish the utility of this formulation from claims of historical priority for its ingredients; no firstness claim is made for formula-valued matrices, logical bra--matrix--ket notation or pointwise operations on logical operators in general.

These paragraphs are suggested replacement language, not a rewritten manuscript or a claim that the requested revision has already been applied. The delivered source remains unchanged.

